.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-browser 1  "rev-stealth-browser " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-browser \- Stealth browser operations (launch a profile, run a stealth\-test sweep)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth browser\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stealth\-browser operations via chromiumoxide. `launch` boots a fingerprint\-cloaked Chrome, navigates, and dumps page metadata; `stealth\-test` runs a detection\-page sweep (default bot.sannysoft.com).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rev\-stealth\-browser\-launch(1)
Launch a stealth browser, navigate to a URL, and emit JSON about the resulting page (UA / viewport / title / final URL). Useful as a smoke test that the launcher works on this host
.TP
rev\-stealth\-browser\-stealth\-test(1)
Run a stealth self\-test: launch a stealth browser, navigate to the target detection page (defaults to bot.sannysoft.com), wait briefly, then dump UA / viewport / title
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth browser launch \-\-profile mobile\-ios \-\-url https://example.com
  $ rev\-stealth browser stealth\-test \-\-dwell 5

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Browser action completed.
  1  UserError        Unknown \-\-profile or \-\-stealth slug.
  2  TransientError   Chrome launch / CDP transient failure.
  3  PermanentError   Chrome binary missing or stealth level unsupported.

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_CHROME  Override the chrome executable path.
